%% Generic pointer session lifecycle state diagram
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Idle

  state "Idle / no routed pointer" as Idle
  note right of Idle
    No active pointer token, session id, tool session,
    or pointer-owned preview snapshot exists.
    A runtime admits at most one routed pointer session.
  end note

  Idle --> Disposed: runtime.dispose()
  Idle --> Idle: stale move/up/cancel / ignore
  Idle --> AdmissionGate: handlePointer(down)
  Idle --> Idle: non-down sample without active token / ignore

  state "Down admission gate" as AdmissionGate
  note right of AdmissionGate
    The surface pointer adapter routes samples through
    the runtime-surface port.
    Down samples must be normalized and finite before
    InteractionEngine admits a pointer token.
    Invalid down facts are rejected before runtime routing.
    Invalid terminal facts for an active route enter cleanup only.
  end note

  AdmissionGate --> ActivePointer: finite normalized down / bind token, session id, and controllerEpoch
  AdmissionGate --> Idle: non-finite or invalid down / reject without preview
  AdmissionGate --> Disposed: runtime disposed / StateError

  state "Active pointer / one routed token" as ActivePointer {
    [*] --> Routing

    state "Routed session" as Routing
    note right of Routing
      The active session owns exactly one pointer id,
      session id, and controllerEpoch. Pointer id is a routing
      token only, not document identity.
    end note

    Routing --> Routing: same-token finite move / update preview only
    Routing --> Routing: concurrent down while active / reject without second session
    Routing --> Routing: stale move or controllerEpoch mismatch / ignore without preview, repaint, edit, or event
    Routing --> TerminalGate: same-token up
    Routing --> CleanupOnly: same-token cancel
    Routing --> CleanupOnly: mode/tool change cancels session
    Routing --> CleanupOnly: interactive=false routes cancel for active routed pointer only
    Routing --> CleanupOnly: loadDocument prepared cleanup before install interrupts session
    Routing --> Routing: loadDocumentFromJson failure / preserve active session
    Routing --> DisposeCleanup: runtime.dispose() interrupts session

    state "Terminal sample gate" as TerminalGate
    note right of TerminalGate
      Terminal up samples can commit only when pointer token,
      session id, controllerEpoch, and terminal facts still match.
      Stale terminal facts may release the active token but
      cannot create a commit intent.
      Invalid terminal facts enter cleanup only.
    end note

    TerminalGate --> CleanupOnly: stale token, controllerEpoch mismatch, non-finite facts, or invalid terminal
    TerminalGate --> TerminalDecision: finite same-token terminal facts

    state TerminalDecision <<choice>>
    TerminalDecision --> CleanupOnly: terminal intent is no-op, selected-move conflict, zero selected-move delta, or empty movable set
    TerminalDecision --> MarqueeCommit: qualified marquee terminal intent / direct resolver-exempt route
    TerminalDecision --> MoveResolverBasis: qualified selected move / immutable participant basis and proposed delta
    TerminalDecision --> NonMovePreparation: qualified draw or eraser terminal intent

    state "Resolver-exempt marquee commit" as MarqueeCommit
    note right of MarqueeCommit
      Marquee selection prepares and consumes its exact selection commit
      directly. Its terminal route does not invoke CanvasCommitResolver.
    end note
    MarqueeCommit --> EditKernelCommit: prepare exact selection commit and consume

    state "Non-Move exact preparation" as NonMovePreparation
    note right of NonMovePreparation
      Draw and eraser construct the exact prepared edit and sealed action
      before resolver invocation.
    end note
    NonMovePreparation --> ResolverDecision: send prepared non-Move request

    state "Move resolver basis" as MoveResolverBasis
    note right of MoveResolverBasis
      Move sends only its immutable participant basis and proposed delta to the
      resolver. It does not prepare the exact transform edit before acceptance.
    end note
    MoveResolverBasis --> ResolverDecision: send CanvasMoveCommitRequest

    state "Unified commit resolver decision" as ResolverDecision
    note right of ResolverDecision
      RuntimeRoot sends one immutable CanvasCommitRequest under the mutation
      guard. Non-Move routes arrive with exact preparation already complete;
      Move arrives with its immutable basis and requires a finite non-zero
      replacement delta before exact preparation.
      A returned lease is aborted once whenever installation will not occur.
    end note
    ResolverDecision --> CleanupOnly: CanvasCommitCancel or non-applicable acceptance
    ResolverDecision --> ResolverErrorCleanup: resolver callback or guard failure
    ResolverDecision --> CommitIntent: compatible non-Move acceptance
    ResolverDecision --> MoveExactPreparation: compatible Move acceptance with final delta

    state "Resolver error cleanup" as ResolverErrorCleanup
    note right of ResolverErrorCleanup
      Resolver callback and guard failures are contained by RuntimeRoot.
      They clear the active route through normal cleanup, apply no edit,
      and return a non-application outcome without rethrowing through
      the pointer handling boundary.
    end note
    ResolverErrorCleanup --> CleanupCoordinator: typed cleanup request and contained non-application

    state "Commit intent" as CommitIntent
    note right of CommitIntent
      Commit-capable pointer tools produce an interaction
      commit request that RuntimeRoot delivers through
      EditKernel. InteractionEngine never mutates
      DocumentStoreKernel directly.
    end note

    CommitIntent --> EditKernelCommit: RuntimeRoot consumes prepared interaction edit

    state "Accepted Move exact preparation" as MoveExactPreparation
    note right of MoveExactPreparation
      Only after accepted final delta does Move prepare its exact transform,
      projection, layout data, and action sealing for consumption.
    end note
    MoveExactPreparation --> EditKernelCommit: consume prepared Move edit

    state "EditKernel commit outcome" as EditKernelCommit
    note right of EditKernelCommit
      Atomic install, rollback, rejection, and staged action
      publication belong to the prepared EditKernel commit outcome path.
    end note

    EditKernelCommit --> CleanupCoordinator: post-success cleanup request
    EditKernelCommit --> CleanupCoordinator: edit failure cleanup request

    state "Cleanup only" as CleanupOnly
    note left of CleanupOnly
      Cancel, prepared load cleanup, mode change,
      active-pointer interactive=false, dispose, stale terminal, invalid terminal, no-op, and
      non-committing paths create typed cleanup requests with
      cleanup reason and ownership context.
      The unified commit resolver is not called on cancel,
      load, mode, interactive=false, or dispose paths.
    end note

    CleanupOnly --> CleanupCoordinator: typed cleanup request
    DisposeCleanup --> CleanupCoordinator: typed cleanup request before stream close

    state "PointerToolCleanupCoordinator" as CleanupCoordinator
    note left of CleanupCoordinator
      The coordinator owns shared cleanup policy and returns
      an effect-only PointerCleanupOutcome. It clears or
      preserves pending line state from ownership context,
      clears pending context tap history when requested, and
      does not call resolvers, open edits, emit actions,
      publish state, or schedule repaint directly.
    end note

    CleanupCoordinator --> CloseSession: clear preview/session state and release active token

    state "Close pointer session" as CloseSession
    note right of CloseSession
      Preview/session cleanup completes and the active token
      is released before public CanvasRuntimeState, action,
      or repaint effects are published to observers.
    end note

    CloseSession --> CleanupTarget: classify outcome previous preview kind

    state CleanupTarget <<choice>>
    CleanupTarget --> MainSceneCleanup: selected-move preview was active
    CleanupTarget --> OverlayCleanup: overlay preview was active
    CleanupTarget --> NoPreviewCleanup: no visible preview

    state "Main-scene cleanup" as MainSceneCleanup
    state "Overlay cleanup" as OverlayCleanup
    state "No-preview cleanup" as NoPreviewCleanup

    MainSceneCleanup --> PublicSignals: queue main-scene cleanup repaint
    OverlayCleanup --> PublicSignals: queue overlay cleanup repaint
    NoPreviewCleanup --> PublicSignals: no cleanup repaint

    state "Public state/effects after close" as PublicSignals
    PublicSignals --> [*]: publish queued CanvasRuntimeState and repaint effects; action only after successful commit

    EditKernelCommit --> RuntimeSafeError: uncontained preparation or accepted-consume error after cleanup

    state "Runtime-safe error boundary" as RuntimeSafeError
    RuntimeSafeError --> [*]
  }

  ActivePointer --> Idle: terminal or cleanup complete
  ActivePointer --> Disposed: dispose cleanup complete

  state "Disposed runtime" as Disposed
  note right of Disposed
    Later pointer input and mutating public operations throw
    StateError("CanvasRuntime is disposed.") and cannot revive
    or commit a stale pointer session.
  end note

  Disposed --> Disposed: dispose() again / return without side effects
  Disposed --> Disposed: pointer input or mutating operation / StateError

  note left of ActivePointer
    Negative invariants:
    no direct Store mutation from InteractionEngine;
    no multiple active pointer sessions;
    no stale terminal commit;
    no unified commit resolver on cancel, load,
    mode, active-pointer interactive=false, or dispose;
    no cleanup of pending line state that is not owned
    by the active routed pointer session;
  end note
